{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"subscription based pricing subscription based pricing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md","fileName":"Subscription-Based Pricing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Subscription-Based Pricing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:39\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Pricing Models]] · [[Game Revenue and Markets]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Pricing Models","Game Revenue and Markets","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"subscription based pricing subscription based pricing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md","fileName":"Subscription-Based Pricing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Subscription-Based Pricing","heading":"Subscription-Based Pricing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Subscription-based pricing gives access to a service for a recurring charge, usually independent of how fully the consumer uses the allocated capability. The agreement may include a minimum term or a notice period before cancellation.\n\nThe model makes spending predictable but can leave paid capacity unused. It can be applied at any service abstraction or deployment model when the access period is a more useful unit than individual resource consumption.\n\nFor an online game, a subscription creates a continuing obligation to provide reliable access, support, updates, and an experience worth the next payment. It suits ongoing worlds and services better than short, self-contained experiences, and some players resist paying repeatedly for continued access.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Pricing Models","Game Revenue and Markets","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"subscription based pricing subscription based pricing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Subscription-Based Pricing.md","fileName":"Subscription-Based Pricing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Subscription-Based Pricing","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cloudcomputing_mit.epub]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Pricing Models","Game Revenue and Markets","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}